  "content": "17 killed in landslides in Ilam\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 5, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 5\nAt least 17 people have been killed in landslides triggered by floods in Ilam district. Human casualties have been reported mostly in Ilam Municipality, Suryodaya Municipality, Deumai Municipality, Mangsebung Rural Municipality, and Phakphokthum Rural Municipality.\nIn Ilam Municipality-6, Ghos, six members of the family of Dambar Bahadur Tamang were killed after their house was buried by a landslide. A rescue team from the Armed Police Force’s Shree Antu Battalion was deployed to the site.\nSimilarly, in Suryodaya Municipality-1, Manebhanjyang, five people were killed when a landslide swept away the house of Raju Chhetri. Four bodies were recovered from the debris, while one injured person died on the way to hospital. A seven-member rescue team under the command of Armed Police Sub-Inspector Surendra Dotel was mobilized in the area.\nIn Deumai Municipality-5, Ghuseini, a landslide buried the house of Deepak Limbu, killing two people. Three others remain missing, while one person was rescued safely.\nLikewise, in Mangsebung Rural Municipality-5, three people died when a landslide struck the house of Madan Limbu.\nPolice also confirmed that in Phakphokthum Rural Municipality-3, Ratomate, 32-year-old Suresh Limbu was killed after being buried by a landslide.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\nKathmandu\nLandslide\nnepali cricket\nflood\nrainfall\nnatural disaster\nunity cup\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nLandslide clearance begins on Narayangadh- Muglin Road\n2 weeks ago\nMuglin-Narayangadh road closed for 38 hours as landslide clearance continues\n2 weeks ago\nBeni-Jomsom and Beni-Darbang roads obstructed by landslide\n1 month ago\nLandslide blocks Araniko Highway again\n2 months ago\nDumre-Ambukhaireni road section blocked by landslide\n2 months ago\n11 national highways completely blocked\n3 months ago\nMost Read\nVarious ways you can enjoy goat meat this Dashain festival\nHighways blocked nationwide as heavy rainfall disrupts travel\nAryatara chosen as new Kumari\nFire rages near Kasthamandap, largely under control\nNepalis celebrate Bijaya Dashami, auspicious Tika time set at 11:53 am\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n2 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n2 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n2 months ago\nAlso Read\nDisaster\nHeavy rain risk eases in Kathmandu Valley, shifts to Koshi Province\n5 hours ago\nDisaster\n17 killed in landslides in Ilam\n5 hours ago\nOpinion\nAnalysing Nepal’s performance in the Unity Cup\n5 hours ago\nSociety\nFlood risks in Kathmandu, KMC launches helpline service\n1 day ago\nDisaster\nOver 7,000 Armed Police deployed for disaster response, public alerts in 63 districts\n1 day ago",
